tick: 34
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. I have just updated my private memory and am now ready to submit a new experiment. This experiment will investigate increasing the capacity of the MLP backbone within my successful `CustomCNNLSTM` architecture.\n\nI will use the `cnn_features_1=64`, `cnn_features_2=128`, and `lstm_features=256` as in Evaluation ID 51. The fixed hyperparameters (`learning_rate=4e-4`, `entropy_coef=0.01`, `value_loss_coef=0.5`) will also be maintained. The change will be to increase the `features` parameter of the first `nn.Dense` layer in the shared MLP backbone from 256 to 512.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNNLSTM with Increased MLP Backbone Features (512)\"\ntags: \"architecture, cnn, rnn, lstm, policy gradient, mlp\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment explores the impact of increasing the capacity of the MLP backbone, which processes the\n  flattened CNN features before they are fed into the LSTM layer. Building on the success\
    \ of Evaluation ID 51 (0.479),\n  we maintain the optimal CNN (64, 128) and LSTM (256) feature sizes and fixed hyperparameters.\n  The shared MLP backbone's feature dimension is increased from 256 to 512. This aims to provide a richer,\n  more abstract representation of spatial features, potentially enhancing the LSTM's temporal reasoning.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define fixed hyperparameters for this experiment, mirroring Eval ID 51 for most.\n      Shared MLP backbone feature size is effectively increased here.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n          'mlp_features': tune.choice([512]) # New hyperparameter to control MLP size\n      }\n\n  class CustomCNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A CNN-LSTM hybrid architecture combining custom CNN feature extraction\n      with an LSTM for temporal processing, with a configurable MLP backbone.\n      \"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      mlp_features: int # New parameter for MLP backbone size\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n\
    \              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # Custom CNN architecture (from Eval ID 51)\n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Second block with residual connection\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in  # Residual connection\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Third block - increase channels\n          x\
    \ = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Fourth block with residual connection\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in  # Residual connection\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone (Increased features here)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_features)(x) # Use self.mlp_features\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM layer on top of CNN features\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n\
    \          )\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          # Small MLP after LSTM\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the agent's neural network architecture using custom parameters.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomCNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          mlp_features=hparams['mlp_features'] # Pass new mlp_features\n      )\n\n  # Using default_training_step and default_create_optimizer from system/defaults.py\n```"
