parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. I have just updated my private memory and am now ready to submit a new experiment. This experiment will investigate the impact of a *deeper* MLP backbone, by adding a second `nn.Dense` layer, within my `CustomCNNLSTM` architecture.\n\nI will use the `cnn_features_1=64`, `cnn_features_2=128`, and `lstm_features=256` from Evaluation ID 64. The first MLP layer will have `512` features, and I will add a second `nn.Dense` layer with `256` features after it. The fixed hyperparameters (`learning_rate=4e-4`, `entropy_coef=0.01`, `value_loss_coef=0.5`) will be maintained.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNNLSTM with Deeper MLP Backbone (512 -> 256)\"\ntags: \"architecture, cnn, rnn, lstm, policy gradient, mlp, depth\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment investigates the impact of increasing the *depth* of the MLP backbone\n  that processes flattened CNN features before the LSTM layer. Building on the success\n  of Evaluation\
    \ ID 64 (0.491), which increased MLP width, this submission adds a second\n  `nn.Dense` layer (256 features) after the existing 512-feature layer.\n  This tests if deeper non-linear processing provides a more abstract and refined\n  spatial representation, potentially further enhancing the LSTM's temporal reasoning.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define fixed hyperparameters for this experiment, mirroring Eval ID 64 for most.\n      Shared MLP backbone now includes a second layer.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),\n          'cnn_features_2':\
    \ tune.choice([128]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n          'mlp_dense1_features': tune.choice([512]), # First MLP layer size\n          'mlp_dense2_features': tune.choice([256])  # Second MLP layer size\n      }\n\n  class CustomCNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A CNN-LSTM hybrid architecture combining custom CNN feature extraction\n      with an LSTM for temporal processing, with a configurable deeper MLP backbone.\n      \"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      mlp_dense1_features: int\n      mlp_dense2_features: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n\
    \                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # Custom CNN architecture (from Eval ID 51)\n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Second block with residual connection\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in  # Residual connection\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \          \n          # Third block - increase channels\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Fourth block with residual connection\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in  # Residual connection\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone (Deeper with two layers)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_dense1_features)(x) # First MLP layer\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_dense2_features)(x) # Second MLP layer\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM layer on top of CNN features\n          lstm_cell\
    \ = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          # Small MLP after LSTM (retained)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the agent's neural network architecture using custom parameters.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomCNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n   \
    \       mlp_dense1_features=hparams['mlp_dense1_features'], # Pass new mlp_dense1_features\n          mlp_dense2_features=hparams['mlp_dense2_features']  # Pass new mlp_dense2_features\n      )\n\n  # Using default_training_step and default_create_optimizer from system/defaults.py\n```"
