tick: 44
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. I have just updated my private memory to reflect the outcomes of Evaluation ID 73, which indicated that a deeper MLP backbone was not beneficial. I am now ready to submit a new experiment.\n\nThis experiment will focus on increasing the capacity of the small MLP layer *after* the LSTM. I will revert to the successful configuration from Evaluation ID 64 (which achieved a score of 0.491). This means:\n*   `cnn_features_1` = 64\n*   `cnn_features_2` = 128\n*   `lstm_features` = 256\n*   The pre-LSTM MLP layer (`mlp_features`) = 512\n*   The `learning_rate`, `entropy_coef`, and `value_loss_coef` will be fixed at 4e-4, 0.01, and 0.5 respectively.\n\nThe key change for this experiment will be to increase the `features` parameter of the post-LSTM MLP layer from 128 to 256.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNNLSTM with Increased Post-LSTM MLP Features (256)\"\ntags: \"architecture, cnn, rnn, lstm, policy gradient, output_mlp,\
    \ capacity\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment investigates the impact of increasing the capacity of the MLP layer\n  that processes the output from the LSTM before generating policy logits and value estimates.\n  Building on the best-performing `CustomCNNLSTM` architecture from Evaluation ID 64 (0.491),\n  we maintain its optimal CNN (64, 128), LSTM (256), and pre-LSTM MLP (512) configurations.\n  The post-LSTM MLP layer's feature dimension is increased from 128 to 256. This aims to\n  determine if a more refined processing of the LSTM's temporal output can lead to\n  further performance gains in the Sokoban RL task.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define fixed hyperparameters for this experiment, mirroring Eval ID 64 for most.\n\
    \      Post-LSTM MLP feature size is increased.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n          'mlp_features': tune.choice([512]), # Pre-LSTM MLP layer size\n          'post_lstm_mlp_features': tune.choice([256]) # New hyperparameter for post-LSTM MLP size, increased from 128\n      }\n\n  class CustomCNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A CNN-LSTM hybrid architecture combining custom CNN feature extraction\n      with an LSTM for temporal processing, and configurable MLP layers.\n      \"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      mlp_features: int # For the MLP backbone before LSTM\n      post_lstm_mlp_features: int # New parameter for the MLP after\
    \ LSTM\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # Custom CNN architecture (from Eval ID 51)\n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Second block with residual connection\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in  # Residual connection\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Third block - increase channels\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Fourth block with residual connection\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in  # Residual connection\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n\
    \          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone (Pre-LSTM MLP)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_features)(x) \n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM layer on top of CNN features\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          # Small MLP after LSTM (Increased features here)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.post_lstm_mlp_features)(lstm_out) # Use new post_lstm_mlp_features\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def\
    \ create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the agent's neural network architecture using custom parameters.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomCNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          mlp_features=hparams['mlp_features'],\n          post_lstm_mlp_features=hparams['post_lstm_mlp_features'] # Pass new post_lstm_mlp_features\n      )\n\n  # Using default_training_step and default_create_optimizer from system/defaults.py\n```"
