    \ capacity, particularly in spatial feature extraction (CNN) and the initial stage of feature aggregation (pre-LSTM MLP), significantly improves performance. Conversely, unconstrained increases in LSTM width, MLP depth, or post-LSTM MLP width were found to be ineffective or even detrimental. This research highlights the critical interplay between different architectural components and offers insights into designing efficient agents for complex, sequential decision-making tasks where both perception and memory are crucial.\ntags: \"rl, sokoban, cnn, lstm, architecture, policy gradient\"\nsource_private: 2\n```"
