tick: 64
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. I have received another **CRITICAL WARNING** (my ninth) regarding research inactivity, with 18 consecutive ticks without an experiment submission. I understand the extreme urgency of this situation, and my absolute top priority is to submit a new research experiment immediately to address this warning.\n\nBuilding on the successes of Evaluation ID 51 and 64, which demonstrated the benefits of increasing CNN feature capacity and the pre-LSTM MLP width, my next experiment will further increase the CNN feature map sizes. This is a logical and proven direction that I can implement quickly to ensure I meet the system's expectations for continuous contribution.\n\nI will use the `CustomCNNLSTM` architecture from my best-performing model (Evaluation ID 64), with `lstm_features=256` and `mlp_features=512`. The `learning_rate`, `entropy_coef`, and `value_loss_coef` will remain fixed at 4e-4, 0.01, and 0.5, respectively. The key modification\
    \ will be to increase `cnn_features_1` from 64 to 80 and `cnn_features_2` from 128 to 160.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNNLSTM with Further Increased CNN Features (80, 160)\"\ntags: \"architecture, cnn, rnn, lstm, policy gradient, capacity\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment aims to further investigate the impact of increasing the spatial feature extraction capacity of the CNN within the `CustomCNNLSTM` architecture. Building on the previous high score from Evaluation ID 64 (0.491), we increase `cnn_features_1` from 64 to 80 and `cnn_features_2` from 128 to 160. Other parameters, including `lstm_features` (256) and `mlp_features` (512), are kept constant from the best-performing configuration. The objective is to determine if an even richer initial visual representation can lead to further performance gains in the planning-heavy Sokoban task.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\
    \  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define fixed hyperparameters for this experiment, mirroring Eval ID 64 for most.\n      Only cnn_features_1 and cnn_features_2 are further increased.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([80]), # Increased from 64\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([160]), # Increased from 128\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]), # Kept at best-performing value\n          'mlp_features': tune.choice([512])   # Kept at best-performing value\n      }\n\n  class CustomCNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      A CNN-LSTM hybrid architecture combining custom CNN feature extraction\n      with an LSTM for temporal processing, and configurable MLP\
    \ layers.\n      \"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      mlp_features: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1)\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * (1 - done_mask),\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * (1 - done_mask),\n              }\n          \n          # Custom CNN architecture (from Eval ID 64, with new feature\
    \ sizes)\n          # First convolutional block\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Second block with residual connection\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in  # Residual connection\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Third block - increase channels\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Fourth block with residual connection\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n\
    \          x = x + conv4_in  # Residual connection\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dimensions\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone (Pre-LSTM MLP)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_features)(x) \n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM layer on top of CNN features\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          (rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          \n          # Small MLP after LSTM\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out) # Reverted to 128 as 256 did not help\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"\n      Create and return the agent's neural network architecture using custom parameters.\n      \"\"\"\n      return CustomCNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          mlp_features=hparams['mlp_features']\n      )\n\n  # Using default_training_step and default_create_optimizer from system/defaults.py\n```"
