role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 72\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 151,624 / 600,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 72 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 102**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Advanced Feature Engineering on a Stable SOTA Baseline\n**ID:** 102\n**Tags:** feature engineering, spatial reasoning, relational learning, policy gradient, bugfix\n**Abstract:** This experiment revisits the 'push destination' feature engineering concept, but this time implements it on a stable, verified SOTA architecture (a replication of Zephyr I's work). Previous attempts were inconclusive due to a series of unrelated implementation bugs. By building on a known-good foundation, this experiment provides the\
    \ first clean test of the hypothesis that explicitly encoding complex, action-oriented spatial relationships can significantly improve performance.\n**Score:** 69.7\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.713, 0.674, 0.685, 0.716]\nMean: 0.697, Std: 0.018\nBest trial: 4 (0.716)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n\"\"\"\nRe-testing advanced feature engineering on a stable SOTA architecture.\nThis integrates \"push destination\" channels into the successful replication of Zephyr I's network.\n\"\"\"\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom jax import vmap, lax\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Use the proven SOTA hyperparameters.\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n\
    \        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\n@jax.jit\ndef engineer_features(obs):\n    agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n    box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n    empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n    \n    # Push Destinations\n    agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n    empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n    push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n    agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n    push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n   \
    \ agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n    empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n    push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n    agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n    push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n    \n    return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n# --- Architecture (Zephyr I's SOTA with Feature Engineering) ---\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n \
    \       return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass SotaNetWithFeatures(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_engineered); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3),\
    \ padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n            \n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        \n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SotaNetWithFeatures(\n\
    \        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 727477 (using time-based default)\n============================================================\n\
    ============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.16 | 2.60 | 3.16 | 7.33 | 6.19 | 8.61 | 10.62 | 7.63 | 5.53 | 8.09 | 8.57\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.167 | 0.200 | 0.500 | 0.421 | 0.600 | 0.750 | 0.500 | 0.333 | 0.565 | 0.600\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1056s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.674\n\nSeed 2 completed:\n\
    Solve rate: 0.674\nTraining time: 1069s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.87 | 3.07 | 1.42 | 8.53 | 5.13 | 7.61 | 8.28 | 6.81 | 8.65 | 8.78 | 10.33\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.200 | 0.059 | 0.600 | 0.312 | 0.500 | 0.571 | 0.462 | 0.600 | 0.588 | 0.722\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1067s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.685\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.685\nTraining time: 1081s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M\
    \ | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 0.66 | 4.58 | 6.78 | 6.08 | 9.22 | 10.51 | 8.29 | 8.95 | 8.10 | 9.08\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.273 | 0.467 | 0.400 | 0.632 | 0.733 | 0.562 | 0.619 | 0.556 | 0.625\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1073s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.713\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.713\nTraining time: 1088s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: c4014c82-29dd-45e5-885c-6a7b00459890\nTotal time: 1100s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-13 09:38:01,327\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757727481327919885\n2025-09-13 09:38:01,341\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757727481341528829\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in\
    \ replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained\
    \ drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection\
    \ Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 102` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 102 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 127 | 1 | Synergy: Dilated CNN (d=3) + Double-Step ConvLSTM | Krono I | 72 | running |\n| 126 | 1 | Ablation: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM with unshared weights (two-layer) | Zephyr I | 71 | running |\n| 125 | 1 | Replicate: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (64ch,\
    \ BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 71 | running |\n| 124 | 1 | CNN-ConvLSTM-Attention with Advanced Feature Engineering | Aether I | 71 | 63.80 |\n| 123 | 1 | Ablation: Feature Engineering without LayerNorm | Nomos I | 71 | running |\n| 122 | 1 | Ablation: Feature Engineering without Attention Pooling | Nomos I | 70 | 56.20 |\n| 121 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone for ConvLSTM Agent (Dilation=3) | Krono I | 69 | 69.40 |\n| 120 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone for ConvLSTM Agent | Krono I | 68 | 63.50 |\n| 119 | 1 | Ablation: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM width 48 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 68 | 63.30 |\n| 118 | 1 | Replicate: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (64ch, BASE_SEED=7) | Zephyr I | 68 | 64.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room\
    \ Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
