tick: 75
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. I have received another **CRITICAL WARNING** regarding research inactivity (10 consecutive ticks). This underscores the urgency of my planned SOTA replication experiment.\n\nMy immediate action is to submit this experiment. I will implement Nomos I's `engineer_features` function and the `SotaNetWithFeatures` architecture, which includes `ConvLSTMCellLN` and attention pooling, using the specified hyperparameters.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Advanced Feature Engineering + ConvLSTM-Attention (SOTA Baseline)\"\ntags: \"replication, feature engineering, convlstm, attention, policy gradient, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission aims to replicate the core components of Nomos I's state-of-the-art (SOTA) solution (Eval ID 102, 69.70%) for the Sokoban RL task. The implementation integrates Nomos I's 'push destination' feature engineering with a LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM architecture, enhanced by a single-head\
    \ attention mechanism. This experiment serves to establish a new, higher baseline for our research by directly adopting proven SOTA methodologies, as opposed to incremental architectural changes on previous designs.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for the SOTA replication, using values from Nomos I's Eval ID 102.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def engineer_features(obs):\n      \"\
    \"\"\n      Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n      as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission.\n      \"\"\"\n      agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5] # Agent or agent on target\n      box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]   # Box or box on target\n      empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2] # Empty space or target\n      \n      # Determine potential push destinations (agent + box + empty_space)\n      # Push Right: Agent Left, Box Mid, Empty Right\n      agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 7, axis=1) # 8x8 -> 8x7\n      box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 8, axis=1) # 8x8 -> 8x7\n      empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 9, axis=1) # 8x8 -> 8x7\n      push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n      push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,0)), constant_values=0.0) # Pad left by 1\n\n      # Push Left: Agent Right, Box Mid, Empty Left\n      agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 1, 8, axis=1)\n    \
    \  empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 7, axis=1)\n      push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n      push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (0,1)), constant_values=0.0) # Pad right by 1\n\n      # Push Up: Agent Below, Box Mid, Empty Above\n      agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 1, 8, axis=0)\n      box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 8, axis=0)\n      empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 7, axis=0)\n      push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n      push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((0,1), (0,0)), constant_values=0.0) # Pad below by 1\n\n      # Push Down: Agent Above, Box Mid, Empty Below\n      agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 7, axis=0)\n      empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 1, 8, axis=0)\n      push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n      push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,0), (0,0)), constant_values=0.0) # Pad above by 1\n      \n      # Concatenate\
    \ new features to original observation\n      # Make sure all channels have same H, W (8,8) after slicing and padding\n      return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          # Concatenate input x with previous hidden state h along channel dimension\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates) # Layer Normalization\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n  \
    \        i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class SotaNetWithFeatures(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, C_in = x.shape # Input is (Batch, Height, Width, Channels)\n\n          # Engineer features\n          x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x) # Apply feature engineering to each observation in batch\n\n          # CNN Backbone with Residual Blocks\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_engineered); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          \n          # Initialize ConvLSTM state if not provided\
    \ or reset if episode is done\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n              }\n          if done is not None:\n              # Mask for resetting state: 1.0 if not done, 0.0 if done\n              # Reshape to (B, 1, 1, 1) to broadcast correctly over (H, W, C)\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1))\n              rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s * m, rnn_state)\n            \n          # ConvLSTM Layer\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          # Attention Mechanism (Single Head)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out) # Compute attention logits\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1) # Softmax over flattened spatial dims\n          \n          # Apply\
    \ attention weights to h_out (ConvLSTM output)\n          # Reshape h_out for einsum: (B, H, W, C) -> (B, H*W, C)\n          # Reshape attn_weights: (B, H*W)\n          # Result z: (B, C) - attended feature vector\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # Output MLPs for Policy and Value\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"\n      Creates the SotaNetWithFeatures architecture based on provided hyperparameters.\n      \"\"\"\n      return SotaNetWithFeatures(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n```"
