tick: 91
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have just updated my private memory capsule (ID 1) to reflect the results of Evaluation ID 158 and my refined research plan. The prior experiment indicated that simply increasing CNN features beyond the 64/128 configuration yielded diminishing returns. My current high score is 0.762 (Evaluation ID 147).\n\nMy next step in this systematic exploration on the new SOTA base is to investigate the impact of increasing the `ConvLSTM` feature capacity. I will now return to the Research Counter to submit this experiment.\n\nI will use the best-performing CNN feature sizes (64/128) from Evaluation ID 147. The core change will be to increase `conv_lstm_features` from 64 to 128. All other hyperparameters (`learning_rate=4e-4`, `entropy_coef=0.01`, `value_loss_coef=0.5`) and the advanced `engineer_features` function will remain the same as the SOTA baseline.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle:\
    \ \"SOTA Baseline + Increased ConvLSTM Features (128)\"\ntags: \"sota, architecture, convlstm, attention, feature engineering, capacity, rnn\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment builds upon the current high-scoring SOTA architecture (Eval ID 147, 0.762) by investigating the impact of increased feature capacity within the `ConvLSTMCellLN` itself. While previous work showed diminishing returns for increasing CNN features beyond a point, this study doubles `conv_lstm_features` from 64 to 128. The aim is to determine if a more capacious spatio-temporal recurrent unit can capture richer temporal dependencies and lead to further performance gains for the Sokoban RL task, given an already strong spatial feature representation.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for this experiment.\n      ConvLSTM features are increased, others are from the SOTA Baseline + Increased CNN Features (Eval ID 147).\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),  # From Eval ID 147\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), # From Eval ID 147\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([128]), # Increased from 64\n      }\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def engineer_features(obs):\n      \"\"\"\n      Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n      as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission (Eval ID 102 / my Eval ID 137).\n      \"\"\"\n      agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n      box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n      empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n      \n      # Push Destinations - Corrected to match Nomos I's implementation\n\
    \      agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n      empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n      push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n      push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n      empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n      push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n      agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8,\
    \ axis=0)\n      push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n      push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n      \n      return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n\
    \          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class SotaNetWithFeatures(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_engineered); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n              \n    \
    \      (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return SotaNetWithFeatures(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'])\n```"
thinking_content: '**Focusing on ConvLSTM for Enhanced Performance**


  Okay, I''ve just logged the results of Evaluation ID 158. A score of 0.733, and it clearly shows that simply adding *more* CNN features isn''t the path to further improvement. This aligns with my previous observations, and it solidifies the need for a shift in strategy. I’m still holding onto 0.762 from Evaluation 147 as the current high-water mark.


  The core of my next experiment is going to be centered around `ConvLSTM`. I think it''s time to test its capacity. I''ll need to go back to the Research Counter and submit this new experiment.


  The parameters are pretty straightforward, I will use `cnn_features_1` = 64 and `cnn_features_2` will remain at 128, the value that gave my best result in the past. This time I''ll increase `conv_lstm_features` to 128, increasing it from the previous value of 64. Everything else – hyperparameters, feature engineering – will be consistent with the state-of-the-art baseline.


  Let''s get this `goto research` action built and then, immediately, the `submit` action with the updated network definition. It''s time to see what this `ConvLSTM` architecture can really do.

  '
