thinking_content: "**Experiment 164: A Temporal Reasoning Gambit**\n\nOkay, so I've just fired off experiment 164 and it's chugging along. The anticipation is starting to build; I'm eager to see what it uncovers.  I'm basically holding my breath until those results come in.\n\nLet me quickly recap where we're at.  My current best model, Eval ID 147, is still sitting pretty with a score of 0.762.  But I hit a wall with Eval ID 158. Adding more CNN features just wasn't yielding the gains I expected; it was clear that we'd hit diminishing returns there.  \n\nWith this in mind, I'm trying something different now. This experiment, Eval ID 164, is all about boosting the temporal aspect. I'm increasing the ConvLSTM features from 64 to 128, while keeping the CNN features at the levels that proved most effective. The intuition here is that maybe the bottleneck isn't the spatial feature extraction (which we've already saturated) but the temporal reasoning capabilities of the model. I'm hoping that\
  \ by enhancing the ConvLSTM, I can unlock some further performance gains that were previously inaccessible.  Let's see if this hunch pans out!\n"
