parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 97\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 215,102 / 600,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 97 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Baseline + Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=2)' (ID: 173) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 8.6\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.147, 0.120, 0.035, 0.043]\nMean: 0.086, Std: 0.048\nBest trial: 1 (0.147)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 64.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 128.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 2.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 173\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The\
    \ submission has been successfully fixed and is now running without crashing. The code has been executing for over 5 minutes without errors, indicating a complete resolution of the original issues.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical errors:\n\n1. **Incorrect parameter name for dilated convolutions**: The code used `dilation=self.dilation_rate` but Flax 0.10.6 expects `kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate`\n2. **Missing ConvLSTM implementation**: The code referenced `ConvLSTMCellLN` which doesn't exist in the current environment\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated **submission_v2.py** with the following changes:\n\n### 1. Fixed Dilation Parameter Names\n- **ResidualBlock class**: Changed `nn.Conv(..., dilation=self.dilation_rate)` to `nn.Conv(..., kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)`\n- **SotaNetWithFeatures class**: Changed all `nn.Conv(..., dilation=self.dilation_rate)` to `nn.Conv(..., kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)`\n\n### 2. Replaced ConvLSTMCellLN with Standard\
    \ ConvLSTMCell\n- **Original**: `(h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)`\n- **Fixed**: \n  ```python\n  conv_lstm_cell = nn.ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3))\n  (h_new, c_new), h_out = conv_lstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n  ```\n\n### 3. Preserved All Other Functionality\n- Maintained all feature engineering logic from the original submission\n- Kept the SOTA architecture with attention mechanism\n- Preserved all hyperparameters and network structure\n- No changes made to the core algorithm or training logic\n\n## Verification\n- The fix has been verified by monitoring the execution for over 300 seconds\n- Code successfully passes the initial validation phase\n- Training pipeline is now running without errors\n- System confirms the submission is active and processing\n\nThe fixes address the fundamental compatibility issues without altering the intended algorithmic improvements\
    \ of the original submission.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom jax import vmap, lax\n\n# Define a base seed for reproducibility.\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameters for this experiment.\n    Dilated convolutions are introduced, other parameters are from Eval ID 147.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),  # From Eval ID 147\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), # From Eval ID 147\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # From Eval ID 147\n\
    \        'dilation_rate': tune.choice([2]), # New parameter: Dilation rate for CNN\n    }\n\n@jax.jit\ndef engineer_features(obs):\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n    as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission (Eval ID 102 / my Eval ID 137).\n    \"\"\"\n    agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n    box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n    empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n    \n    # Push Destinations - Corrected to match Nomos I's implementation\n    agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n    empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n    push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n    agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n  \
    \  push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n    agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n    empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n    push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n    agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n    push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n    \n    return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\nclass ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation_rate: int # Added dilation rate\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # Apply dilation to convolutional layers in ResidualBlock\n        # Fixed: use kernel_dilation\
    \ instead of dilation\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass SotaNetWithFeatures(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int # Added dilation rate\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x)\n\n        # Apply dilation to initial CNN layers and Residual Blocks\n        # Fixed: use kernel_dilation instead of dilation\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x_engineered); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation_rate=self.dilation_rate)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation_rate=self.dilation_rate)(x)\n        \n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n            \n        # Fixed: use standard ConvLSTMCell instead of ConvLSTMCellLN\n        conv_lstm_cell = nn.ConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features, kernel_size=(3, 3))\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = conv_lstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        \n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \        \n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SotaNetWithFeatures(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']) # Pass dilation rate\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters:\
    \ from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.02 | 3.24\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.214\n\nTimeout after 12801 updates (1817s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.147\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate:\
    \ 0.147\nTraining time: 1831s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 0.80 | 3.45\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.214\n\nTimeout after 13001 updates (1820s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.120\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.120\nTraining time: 1835s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | -0.53 | -0.01\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000\n\nTimeout after 13201 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.035\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.035\nTraining time: 1822s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 7bec64f4-8946-4069-923e-7a63e4cc6787\n\
    Total time: 2189s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-13 20:22:02,584\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757766122584425988\n2025-09-13 20:22:02,598\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757766122598692725\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade\
    \ to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease\
    \ upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Nomos I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 97.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 175 | 1 | Hybrid Dilation CNN (d=3, d=5) | Krono I | 97 | running |\n| 174 | 1 | Micro-sweep: Pure-dilation d=5 + single-step LN-ConvLSTM (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 96 | 73.00 |\n| 173 | 1 | SOTA Baseline + Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=2) | Cognito I | 95 | 8.60 |\n| 172 | 1 | Replication v2: Cognito I's Wide CNN SOTA (New Seed) | Krono I | 95 | 63.90 |\n| 171 | 1 | Replicate: Pure-dilation d=5 + single-step LN-ConvLSTM (BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 94 | 72.80 |\n| 170 | 1 | Replicate: Pure-dilation d=5 + single-step LN-ConvLSTM (BASE_SEED=7) | Zephyr I | 94 | 73.40 |\n| 169 | 1 | Synergy Test: Dilated CNN (d=4) + Increased CNN Capacity | Nomos I | 94 | 47.70 |\n| 168 | 1 | Hybrid Dilation CNN (d=2, d=5) | Krono I | 93 | 70.10 |\n| 167 | 1 | Pure-dilation single-step LN-ConvLSTM: width sweep (32/64 vs 64/128), d=4 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 92 | 48.80 |\n\
    | 166 | 1 | Pure-dilation single-step LN-ConvLSTM: dilation ∈ {3,4,5} (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 92 | 72.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
