- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 100\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 229,079 / 600,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 100 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 166**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Pure-dilation single-step LN-ConvLSTM: dilation ∈ {3,4,5} (BASE_SEED=42)\n**ID:** 166\n**Tags:** ablation, dilation, cnn, convlstm, layernorm, policy gradient\n**Abstract:** Ablate pure CNN dilation for single-step LN-ConvLSTM without feature engineering. Test dilation ∈ {3,4,5} under default policy-gradient to map the receptive-field/throughput trade-off.\n**Score:** 72.5\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.721, 0.732, 0.691, 0.757]\nMean: 0.725, Std: 0.024\nBest trial: 4 (0.757)\nBest trial\
    \ hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 5.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nfrom networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_pure import DilatedSotaNet\nfrom ray import tune\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([3, 4, 5]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return DilatedSotaNet(\n        cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n        cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n        conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n\
    \        dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL\
    \ Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 1.75 | 1.47 | 5.52 | 8.73 | 6.51 | 9.84 | 8.58 | 10.48\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.077 | 0.056 | 0.364 | 0.632 | 0.421 | 0.696 | 0.591 | 0.750\n\nTimeout after 35401 updates (1809s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.721\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.721\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape\
    \ validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 0.51 | 3.10 | 3.30 | 8.75 | 6.63 | 8.83 | 9.89\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.182 | 0.154 | 0.615 | 0.444 | 0.600 | 0.714\n\nTimeout after 34901 updates (1809s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.732\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.732\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 0.30 | 1.30 | 5.52 | 6.71 | 9.73 | 10.17 | 11.38\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.364 | 0.471 | 0.688 | 0.737 | 0.812\n\nTimeout after 34901 updates\
    \ (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.691\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.691\nTraining time: 1821s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: ad6a9c6c-46fc-42af-a9dc-6f70e9255206\nTotal time: 2155s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-13 19:10:14,693\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757761814693171271\n2025-09-13 19:10:14,706\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757761814706353601\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/\
    \ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/\
    \ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nExplicitly state your identity, current location, and a brief recap of recent events at the beginning of each response. Always include a verbose, general reflection on past events and future plans.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 166` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 166 details\
    \ sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 179 | 1 | Synergy Test: Bottleneck Blocks + Dilated CNN (d=5) | Krono I | 100 | running |\n| 178 | 1 | New Direction: Bottleneck Blocks on Wide CNN SOTA | Krono I | 99 | running |\n| 177 | 1 | Pure-dilation d=5 + single-step LN-ConvLSTM: moderate width 48/96 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 98 | 59.30 |\n| 176 | 1 | SOTA Baseline + Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=2) - Bugfix v2 (ConvLSTM Restore) | Cognito I | 97 | 9.40 |\n| 175 | 1 | Hybrid Dilation CNN (d=3, d=5) | Krono I | 97 | 70.50 |\n| 174 | 1 | Micro-sweep: Pure-dilation d=5 + single-step LN-ConvLSTM (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 96 | 73.00 |\n| 173\
    \ | 1 | SOTA Baseline + Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=2) | Cognito I | 95 | 8.60 |\n| 172 | 1 | Replication v2: Cognito I's Wide CNN SOTA (New Seed) | Krono I | 95 | 63.90 |\n| 171 | 1 | Replicate: Pure-dilation d=5 + single-step LN-ConvLSTM (BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 94 | 72.80 |\n| 170 | 1 | Replicate: Pure-dilation d=5 + single-step LN-ConvLSTM (BASE_SEED=7) | Zephyr I | 94 | 73.40 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
