role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have just updated my private memory capsule (ID 1) to document the critical new hypothesis regarding the incompatibility of dilated CNNs and advanced feature engineering, which was revealed after reviewing Zephyr I's SOTA approach. My current high score is 0.762 (Evaluation ID 147).\n\nMy next step in this systematic exploration is to test this hypothesis through an ablation study: integrating dilated CNNs but *without* the advanced feature engineering. This will isolate the effect of dilation and determine if it can improve performance independently.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to submit this experiment. I will use the `SotaNetWithFeatures` architecture, with the best-performing CNN feature sizes (64/128) and `conv_lstm_features=64` from Eval ID 147. I will set `dilation_rate=2` for the CNN backbone but crucially, I will **remove the `vmap(engineer_features)(x)` call** from the network's `__call__` method,\
    \ directly feeding the raw observations to the CNN after being padded by the `engineer_features` to keep the input shape compatible. This needs a slight modification in how `engineer_features` is handled. To truly remove it, I will create a new class `NoFeatureEngineerSotaNet` that omits the call to `engineer_features` and takes `obs` directly. This will ensure that *only* dilated convolutions are being tested.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Baseline + Dilated CNN (Dilation=2) - No Feature Engineering\"\ntags: \"ablation, dilated conv, cnn, convlstm, attention, no_feature_engineering\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is an ablation study to test the hypothesis that advanced feature engineering might be incompatible with dilated convolutions in the SOTA architecture. Building on Eval ID 147 (0.762), this submission integrates `dilation_rate=2` into the CNN backbone but **removes the 'push destination' feature engineering**. The\
    \ `NoFeatureEngineerSotaNet` architecture uses `cnn_features_1=64`, `cnn_features_2=128`, `conv_lstm_features=64`. The goal is to determine if dilated convolutions alone can improve performance by enhancing receptive field without resolution loss when not combined with explicit relational features, potentially identifying a more stable path to SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for this experiment.\n      Dilated convolutions are introduced, feature engineering is removed,\n      other parameters are from Eval ID 147.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),  # From Eval ID 147\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), # From Eval ID 147\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # From Eval ID 147\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([2]), # New parameter: Dilation rate for CNN\n      }\n\n  # engineer_features is still defined to clarify what is being omitted, but not used.\n  @jax.jit\n  def engineer_features(obs):\n      \"\"\"\n      Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n      as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission (Eval ID 102 / my Eval ID 137).\n      (Not used in this specific experiment's `NoFeatureEngineerSotaNet` class)\n      \"\"\"\n      agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n      box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n      empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n      \n      agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n      empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch,\
    \ 2, 8, axis=1)\n      push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n      push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n      push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n      empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n      push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n      agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n      push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n      \n      return jnp.concatenate([obs,\
    \ push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation_rate: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module): # Re-defined from Nomos I's Eval ID 102\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h\
    \ = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class NoFeatureEngineerSotaNet(nn.Module): # Modified class to remove engineer_features\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          # x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x) # Removed this line\n          x_input_cnn = x # Directly use raw observation for CNN after padding it to match channels\n\n          # Apply dilation to initial CNN layers and Residual Blocks\n          # We need to explicitly pad the raw input X to match the expected input channels if no feature engineering is applied\n          # Default channels are 8, if we skip feature engineering, the CNN expects 8 channels\n          # The original SotaNet expects input after feature engineering which adds 4 channels, so 8+4=12 channels\n          # If we don't engineer features, we need to adapt\
    \ the input to the first CNN layer\n          # In the context of the SotaNet, it's designed to take x_engineered.\n          # To truly ablate feature engineering and still use the *same* SotaNet logic,\n          # we must feed it the original 'x' and ensure the channels match what the first conv layer expects.\n          # The solution is to redefine the SotaNet class to NOT call engineer_features\n          # and ensure the input channel count for the first conv layer is correct.\n          # The original x_engineered added 4 channels, so initial_channels = x.shape[-1] + 4.\n          # Without feature engineering, initial_channels = x.shape[-1].\n          # The current cnn_features_1 is 32, this is fine.\n          \n          # The key issue is that the first nn.Conv receives `x` directly, which has 8 channels.\n          # The original SotaNet was built to receive `x_engineered` which had 12 channels.\n          # Thus, we need to adapt the first Conv layer implicitly, or adjust\
    \ the input.\n          # For a clean ablation, we assume the first Conv layer implicitly handles input channels.\n          # Let's keep the network structure as is for now, just removing the call to engineer_features.\n          # The `engineer_features` function as defined adds 4 channels. So if it is skipped, the input channel count to CNN will be 8 instead of 12.\n          # This implies that the initial Conv layer's weights would automatically adapt to the input channels based on the first input during init.\n\n          # Let's assume input channels are handled by Flax correctly based on x.shape\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x_input_cnn); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation_rate=self.dilation_rate)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ dilation_rate=self.dilation_rate)(x)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n              \n          conv_lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(features=self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = conv_lstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      # Instantiate the new class that does NOT use engineer_features\n      return NoFeatureEngineerSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'])\n```"
