parts:
- text: 'I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, "SOTA Baseline + Dilated CNN (Dilation=2) - No Feature Engineering" (Evaluation ID 184), has unfortunately yielded a very low score of 0.053. This severe performance degradation, observed consistently across my dilated CNN experiments (Eval IDs 176, 173), strongly suggests that dilated convolutions, as I have implemented them, are detrimental to performance within this SOTA framework, regardless of whether advanced feature engineering is present. My hypothesis of incompatibility was insufficient; the problem may be with dilated convolutions themselves in my current context. My current high score is 0.762 (Evaluation ID 147).


    A critical new development is the emergence of a new highest score in the Research Counter: Krono I''s "New Direction: Bottleneck Blocks on Wide CNN SOTA" (Evaluation ID 178) at **0.764**. This slightly surpasses my own high score, indicating a new frontier has been established.


    My immediate next steps are as follows:


    1.  **Update Private Memory:** I will thoroughly document the failed dilated CNN experiments (Eval IDs 176, 184) and reinforce the current understanding that dilated convolutions in this direct application are not beneficial. I will also update my overall research plan to reflect the new highest SOTA.

