parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 109\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 255,539 / 600,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 109 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/krono/bottleneck_sota.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/krono/bottleneck_sota.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author\
    \ | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 192 | 1 | Activation ablation on bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=5): ReLU vs SiLU (single-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 109 | running |\n| 191 | 1 | Bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=5) + single-step LN-ConvLSTM: bottleneck_ratio sweep | Zephyr I | 109 | running |\n| 190 | 1 | Sanity replicate: DilatedSotaNet d=5 (stored module), BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 107 | 72.90 |\n| 189 | 1 | Pure-dilation d=5 + pre-LSTM 1x1 bottleneck (ratio ∈ {0.5, 0.75, 1.0}), single-step LN | Zephyr I | 106 | 69.10 |\n| 188 | 1 | Paper Recovery 2: Bottleneck Blocks on Standard-Width CNN | Krono I | 105 | 75.50 |\n| 187 | 1 | Paper Recovery 1: Wide CNN SOTA Baseline Replication | Krono I | 105 | 63.50 |\n| 186 | 1 | Pure-dilation d=5 single-step LN-ConvLSTM: attention temperature sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 105 | 62.50 |\n| 185 | 1 | Compute reallocation: d=5 wide CNN (64/128) + smaller ConvLSTM (48ch), single-step LN | Zephyr I | 104 | 43.50 |\n| 184 | 1 |\
    \ SOTA Baseline + Dilated CNN (Dilation=2) - No Feature Engineering | Cognito I | 103 | 5.30 |\n| 183 | 1 | Synergy Test: Bottleneck Blocks + Dilated CNN (d=4) | Krono I | 103 | 73.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/krono/bottleneck_sota.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n# Re-using Zephyr's ConvLSTMCellLN as it is a proven component.\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n# My new architectural idea: a Bottleneck Residual Block\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # 1x1 conv to reduce channels, then 3x3 conv, then 1x1 to restore\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x);\
    \ y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n        # Add shortcut connection\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckSOTANet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Wide CNN Backbone with Bottleneck Blocks\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Standard ConvLSTM\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),\
    \ jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n        new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
