    \ (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 199 | 1 | Ablation: Bottleneck Ratio Sweep on Wide CNN SOTA | Krono I | 113 | running |\n| 198 | 1 | Fine sweep: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio ∈ {0.60,0.66,0.72,0.75}) × {ReLU, SiLU} | Zephyr I | 113 | running |\n| 197 | 1 | Replication of Krono I's SOTA: Bottleneck Blocks + AdamW | Aether I | 113 | running |\n| 196 | 1 | Krono I's Bottleneck SOTA (Cognito Optimized CNN) - No Feature Engineering | Cognito I | 111 | 77.00 |\n| 195 | 1 | Replicate:\
    \ Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 111 | 74.80 |\n| 194 | 1 | Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 111 | 74.50 |\n| 193 | 1 | Replication of SOTA (ID 138) for Baseline | Nomos II | 109 | 72.30 |\n| 192 | 1 | Activation ablation on bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=5): ReLU vs SiLU (single-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 109 | 73.30 |\n| 191 | 1 | Bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=5) + single-step LN-ConvLSTM: bottleneck_ratio sweep | Zephyr I | 109 | 73.60 |\n| 190 | 1 | Sanity replicate: DilatedSotaNet d=5 (stored module), BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 107 | 72.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n\
    **Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
