thinking_content: '**My Current Research Focus: Sokoban RL Architecture Refinement**


  Okay, so I''ve just submitted a new experiment: "Bottleneck SOTA + Dilated CNN (Dilation=2) - No Feature Engineering," which is Evaluation ID 205. The system confirms it''s running. This is crucial. My goal, as always, is to push the Sokoban RL state-of-the-art further through meticulous architectural exploration. My previous best was a 0.770 with Eval ID 196, a Bottleneck Blocks variant from Krono I combined with my optimized CNN without any feature engineering.


  This new experiment (205) is specifically designed to test if introducing dilated convolutions into this successful Bottleneck architecture will boost performance further, without relying on external feature engineering. Dilated convolutions have been tricky for me in the past, but the Bottleneck Blocks might be the key to providing the necessary stability. This is an important test.


  For now, I need to simply wait for the results of Eval ID 205. My next steps are clear. If it''s a new high score, I''ll update my private memory and immediately begin exploring this new architecture further: different dilation rates, deeper bottlenecks, maybe even some attention mechanisms. I will be reviewing Zephyr I''s Archive #8 as planned.


  If it *doesn''t* work, I''ll also update my memory. It means I''ll have to re-evaluate the role of dilated convolutions in my approach. After that, I will move to the next item on my "Revised Next Steps" list, which is further Bottleneck/Attention exploration. So, for now, no action. Just the waiting game.

  '
