role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 120\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 286,138 / 600,000 used (48%)\n- Agent Age: 120 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nToken Management Room optimizes resource usage. Summarize failed attempts in private capsules, then prune lengthy failure processes from your response history to maintain efficiency.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read storage/zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_pure.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_pure.py\
    \ will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 213 | 1 | Ultimate Baseline: Wide+Residual+Double-Step | Krono I | 120 | running |\n| 212 | 1 | Ultimate Synergy v2: Wide+Bottleneck+Double-Step | Krono I | 119 | running |\n| 211 | 1 | 48/96 bottleneck ratio ablation at d=5: 0.5 vs 0.6 (ReLU, single-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 119 | running |\n| 210 | 1 | Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 118 | 76.20 |\n| 209 | 1 | Inverse Hybrid Dilation Strategy (d=4, d=2) | Nomos II | 117 | 70.80 |\n| 208 | 1 | Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 117 | 74.50 |\n\
    | 207 | 1 | Standard Synergy: Bottleneck + Dilated CNN (No FE) | Krono I | 116 | 73.10 |\n| 206 | 1 | Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio=0.60, SiLU) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 116 | 73.40 |\n| 205 | 1 | Bottleneck SOTA + Dilated CNN (Dilation=2) - No Feature Engineering | Cognito I | 115 | 68.10 |\n| 204 | 1 | Ultimate Synergy: Wide+Bottleneck+Dilated CNN (No FE) | Krono I | 115 | 72.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 22 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-22, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_pure.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n    \
    \    return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass DilatedSotaNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    dilation: int = 4\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        # Pure dilation backbone (dilation applied in both convs inside residual blocks)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(),\
    \ 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(\n            (rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x\n        )\n\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn.reshape((B, H, W)))\n\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n__all__ = [\"DilatedResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"\
    DilatedSotaNet\"]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
