role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have just updated my private memory capsule (ID 1) to incorporate the detailed analysis of my previous failures with dilated CNNs and the new hypothesis regarding the importance of `xavier_uniform` initialization, derived from reviewing Zephyr I's successful implementations. My current high score is 0.770 (Evaluation ID 196).\n\nMy next critical step is to test this hypothesis through a new experiment. I will integrate dilated convolutions into my current high-performing `BottleneckSOTANetAdapted` architecture, but this time, I will explicitly apply `nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()` to all relevant `nn.Conv` and `nn.Dense` layers. This aims to stabilize training and enable dilated convolutions to contribute positively to performance.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter to submit this experiment. I will use the configuration from Eval ID 196 (`cnn_features_1=64`, `cnn_features_2=128`, `conv_lstm_features=64`), `dilation_rate=2`,\
    \ no explicit `engineer_features`, and the `AdamW` optimizer with clipping.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Bottleneck SOTA + Dilated CNN (Dilation=2) + Xavier Init - No Feature Engineering\"\ntags: \"sota, architecture, bottleneck, cnn, convlstm, dilation, xavier_init\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment critically re-evaluates the integration of dilated convolutions into the current high-scoring Bottleneck SOTA architecture (Eval ID 196, 0.770). Following consistent previous failures with dilated CNNs, this study incorporates a crucial change: explicit `nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()` for all `nn.Conv` and `nn.Dense` layers, mirroring successful external implementations. Using `dilation_rate=2` and omitting feature engineering, this aims to test if proper initialization stabilizes training and unlocks the performance benefits of dilated convolutions in this advanced architectural context.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from jax import vmap, lax\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for this experiment.\n      Dilated convolutions are introduced into the Bottleneck SOTA with Xavier initialization.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),  # From Eval ID 196\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]), # From Eval ID 196\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]), # From Eval ID 196\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([2]), # Dilation rate for CNN\n      }\n\n  # engineer_features is not used in this architecture.\n  @jax.jit\n  def engineer_features(obs):\n      \"\"\"\n \
    \     (Not used in this specific experiment's `BottleneckSOTANetAdapted` class)\n      Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels)\n      as seen in Nomos I's SOTA submission.\n      \"\"\"\n      agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n      box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n      empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n      \n      agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n      empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n      push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n      push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      box_mid_ud\
    \ = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n      empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n      push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n      agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n      push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n      \n      return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module): # Re-defined from Nomos I's Eval ID 102\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n\
    \          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i,f,o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module): # From Krono I's bottleneck_sota.py\n      features: int\n      dilation_rate: int \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class BottleneckSOTANetAdapted(nn.Module): # Adapted from Krono I's BottleneckSOTANet\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features:\
    \ int; dilation_rate: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          # NO FEATURE ENGINEERING: directly use raw 8-channel observation\n          x_input_cnn = x \n\n          # 1. Wide CNN Backbone with Bottleneck Blocks (with dilation and Xavier init)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_input_cnn); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation_rate=self.dilation_rate)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation_rate=self.dilation_rate)(x)\n          \n          # 2. Standard ConvLSTM (using LayerNorm-gated\
    \ variant)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          (h_new,c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(rnn_state, x)\n          new_rnn_state = (h_new,c_new)\n\n          # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # 4. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckSOTANetAdapted(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'], dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n```"
