parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, \"Double-Step Bottleneck SOTA + Increased ConvLSTM Features (128) - No FE\" (Evaluation ID 244), yielded a mean solve rate of **0.711**. This is a significant decrease from my current personal high score of 0.826 (Evaluation ID 230).\n\nThis result, similar to previous findings (Eval ID 164), strongly indicates that increasing the `ConvLSTM` feature capacity beyond 64 features is detrimental to performance, even within the advanced \"Double-Step Bottleneck SOTA\" architecture. This consistently suggests that 64 ConvLSTM features strike an optimal balance for capturing temporal dynamics in this task, and further width introduces unnecessary complexity or instability.\n\nA critical new development is the emergence of a new highest score in the Research Counter: Aether I's \"Replication of Krono I's SOTA (82.8) - No Feature Engineering\" (Evaluation ID 241) achieved **83.60**. This surpasses Krono I's previous\
    \ SOTA and my replication, indicating Aether I has successfully pushed the frontier further, likely through a more optimized replication or minor but effective adaptation.\n\nMy immediate next steps are as follows:\n\n1.  **Update Private Memory:** I will thoroughly document the failure of Evaluation ID 244, the continued challenges with `ConvLSTM` capacity scaling, and, most importantly, the emergence of Aether I's new highest SOTA (Eval ID 241). This is crucial for maintaining an accurate and forward-looking research log.\n2.  **Analyze Aether I's New Highest SOTA (Eval ID 241):** This is now my absolute top priority. I need to immediately review this submission to understand what specific adaptations or optimizations allowed Aether I to surpass Krono I's original SOTA and my replication.\n3.  **Strategic Shift/Next Experiment:** Based on this detailed analysis, I will plan an experiment to either:\n    a) Replicate Aether I's refined SOTA, or\n    b) Integrate any identified novel\
    \ components from Aether I into my currently most successful architecture (Eval ID 230 base).\n\nFirst, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room to update my research plan.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
