role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 142\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 353,240 / 600,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 142 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 241**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Replication of Krono I's SOTA (82.8) - No Feature Engineering\n**ID:** 241\n**Tags:** rl, sota-replication, bottleneck, dilated-cnn, double-step, convlstm\n**Abstract:** This experiment re-replicates Krono I's State-of-the-Art (SOTA) of 82.8% (Eval ID 219) by removing the explicit 'push destination' feature engineering from the previously successful architecture (Aether I's Eval ID 223, score 81.2). This aims to confirm the hypothesis that advanced architectural components implicitly capture sufficient relational\
    \ information, making explicit feature engineering redundant or detrimental in this highly optimized setup. The goal is to match or surpass the 82.8% solve rate.\n**Score:** 83.6\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.831, 0.806, 0.877, 0.830]\nMean: 0.836, Std: 0.026\nBest trial: 3 (0.877)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 5.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom jax import vmap, lax # vmap not used in this iteration, but keeping import for consistency if needed\n\nBASE_SEED = 10113 # Matching Krono I's submission\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameters for this experiment, matching Krono I's Eval ID 219.\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n    }\n\n# --- Bottleneck-Dilated Residual Block (Combination of Archive #6 and #7 ideas) ---\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1))(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- ConvLSTM Cell with LayerNorm (from Zephyr I's SOTA, Archive #1) ---\nclass LayerNormConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,\
    \ int] = (3, 3)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n        c, h = carry\n        \n        inputs_h = jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1)\n        \n        gates = nn.Conv(\n            features=4 * self.features,\n            kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n            name=\"gates_conv\"\n        )(inputs_h)\n\n        i, f, o, g = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n        i = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"i_ln\")(i)\n        f = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"f_ln\")(f)\n        o = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"o_ln\")(o)\n        g = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"g_ln\")(g)\n        \n        i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n        f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n        o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = nn.tanh(g)\n\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n        \n        return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n# --- Single-Head Attention Pooling (from Zephyr I's SOTA, Archive #1) ---\nclass SingleHeadAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n\
    \    temperature: float = 1.0\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n        batch_size, H, W, C = x.shape\n        \n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(features=1, kernel_size=(1,1), name=\"attn_logits\")(x)\n        attn_logits_flat = attn_logits.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n        attn_weights_flat = nn.softmax(attn_logits_flat / self.temperature, axis=-1)\n        attn_weights = attn_weights_flat.reshape((batch_size, H, W, 1))\n\n        weighted_features = x * attn_weights\n        pooled_features = jnp.sum(weighted_features, axis=(1, 2))\n        \n        return pooled_features\n\nclass SokobanSOTANet828_NoFE(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    dilation_rate: int\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        # x_engineered = vmap(engineer_features)(x) # REMOVED FEATURE ENGINEERING\n\n        # CNN Feature Extraction with Bottleneck-Dilated\
    \ Blocks (input is now raw observation x)\n        x_cnn = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn) # Use raw x\n        x_cnn = BottleneckDilatedBlock(features=self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x_cnn); x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = BottleneckDilatedBlock(features=self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x_cnn)\n        x_cnn = nn.relu(x_cnn) \n\n        # Initialize RNN state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = {'h':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),'c':jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda s: s*m, rnn_state)\n            \n        # Double-step ConvLSTM\n        convlstm_cell = LayerNormConvLSTMCell(features=self.conv_lstm_features, name=\"convlstm_layer\")\n        (h_step1, c_step1), out_step1\
    \ = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x_cnn)\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = convlstm_cell((h_step1, c_step1), x_cnn)\n        \n        # Attention Pooling\n        attended_features = SingleHeadAttentionPooling()(h_out)\n        \n        # MLP and Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(attended_features); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SokobanSOTANet828_NoFE(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\n\
    PYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10113 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\n\
    Parallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 0.09 | 4.02 | 8.05 | 7.50 | 6.48 | 10.66 | 9.67 | 10.35 | 10.79 | 9.35\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.235 | 0.556 | 0.500 | 0.429 | 0.750 | 0.684 | 0.737 | 0.760 | 0.647\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1663s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.830\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.830\nTraining time: 1679s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output\
    \ shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | 0.87 | 3.69 | 8.37 | 9.95 | 8.31 | 8.12 | 9.87 | 9.48 | 11.19 | 12.14\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.200 | 0.588 | 0.714 | 0.571 | 0.550 | 0.708 | 0.682 | 0.808 | 0.875\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1679s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.831\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.831\nTraining time: 1695s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | 0.50 | 2.14 | 6.82 | 6.34 | 10.94 | 9.62 | 9.71 | 9.88 | 10.03\
    \ | 10.70\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.077 | 0.462 | 0.417 | 0.778 | 0.682 | 0.680 | 0.700 | 0.710 | 0.760\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1697s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.806\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.806\nTraining time: 1713s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | 2.65 | 3.18 | 6.99 | 8.62 | 11.25 | 12.15 | 9.44 | 11.64 | 12.84 | 12.15\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.125 | 0.167 | 0.462 | 0.600 | 0.810 | 0.885 | 0.667 | 0.833 | 0.933 | 0.882\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1706s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.877\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.877\nTraining time: 1722s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: a271ac76-9316-4614-b086-baaab09a3b76\nTotal time: 1729s\n\
    ============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 09:51:21,479\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757814681479285848\n2025-09-14 09:51:21,493\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757814681493649822\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium,\
