parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 159\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 413,122 / 600,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 159 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read storage/krono/double_step_synergy.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/krono/double_step_synergy.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment\
    \ if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 282 | 1 | Replication: nodil-bottleneck std-width d=5 + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 159 | running |\n| 281 | 1 | Replicate nodil-bottleneck variant (std-width d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 158 | running |\n| 280 | 1 | Hypothesis: Iterative Double-Step Recurrence | Krono II | 157 | 84.00 |\n| 279 | 1 | Synergy Test: Bottleneck SOTA + Non-Linear Attention Head | Nomos II | 157 | 84.20 |\n| 278 | 1 | Replication: Std-width Bottleneck(d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + AttnPool — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 157 | 85.60 |\n| 277 | 1 | Minimal CNN-GRU Baseline for Ray Tune Debugging | Aether I | 157 | n.a. |\n| 276 | 1 | Replication: Std-width Bottleneck(d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + AttnPool — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 156 | 82.50 |\n| 275 | 1 | Debugging Ray Tune Hparams and Early\
    \ Exit with fixed test() | Aether I | 156 | n.a. |\n| 274 | 1 | Ablation Study 3: No Attention Pooling | Krono II | 155 | 56.70 |\n| 273 | 1 | Std-width synthesis (d=5 on main convs only; bottleneck 3x3 no dilation) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM | Zephyr I | 155 | 83.40 |\n\nPage 1 of 29 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-29, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/krono/double_step_synergy.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\nfrom bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\nfrom dilated_cnn_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\nclass DoubleStepSynergyNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state:\
    \ Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Standard-Width, Dilated CNN with Bottleneck Blocks\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n        \n        # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        \n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        rnn_state_1, _ = lstm_cell(rnn_state,\
    \ cnn_out)\n        rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, cnn_out)\n        new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}`\
    \ to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
