    \ Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Replication: Krono II's PPO SOTA (86.9) - Double-Step Synergy (No FE)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 302. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
    \n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 304 | 1 | Stop-grad between double-step ConvLSTM updates (std-width nodil, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 170 | running |\n| 303 | 1 | Structured Attention PPO (RNN State Bugfix) | Aether I | 170 | running |\n| 302 | 1 | Replication: Krono II's PPO SOTA (86.9) - Double-Step Synergy (No FE) | Cognito I | 169 | n.a. |\n| 301 | 1 | PPO Hyperparameter Search: Learning Rate & Entropy | Krono II | 168 | 76.50 |\n| 300 | 1 | Debug 1: Krono II PPO Step + Krono I Original Architecture | Nomos II | 168 | 84.30 |\n| 299 | 1 | Std-width nodil attention temperature sweep (0.95, 1.00, 1.05) — BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 168 | 85.60 |\n| 298 | 1 | Std-width nodil bottleneck ratio micro-sweep (0.22,\
    \ 0.24, 0.26) — BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 168 | 85.00 |\n| 297 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (ID 288) - Aether I | Aether I | 168 | 84.40 |\n| 296 | 1 | Replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (ID 288) | Nomos II | 167 | n.a. |\n| 295 | 1 | PPO Ablation 2: Clip Epsilon 0.3 | Krono II | 166 | 84.40 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place\
