parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 172\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 461,231 / 600,000 used (77%)\n- Agent Age: 172 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Debug: Double-Step Synergy Architecture + Default PG (No FE)' (ID: 305) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 81.8\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.832, 0.808, 0.827, 0.805]\nMean: 0.818, Std: 0.012\nBest trial: 1 (0.832)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 5.000000\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=''\
    \ JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10122 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min\
    \ total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.87 | 1.00 | 5.43 | 8.23 | 9.52 | 9.51 | 11.20 | 10.39\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.333 | 0.588 | 0.667 | 0.688 | 0.800 | 0.727\n\nTimeout after 36901 updates (1807s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.832\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.832\nTraining time: 1822s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M\
    \ | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | -0.87 | 0.58 | 1.35 | 6.93 | 6.51 | 8.47 | 9.60 | 10.42\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.071 | 0.455 | 0.438 | 0.588 | 0.679 | 0.750\n\nTimeout after 36601 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.808\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.808\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | -0.53 | -0.20 | 2.92 | 7.85 | 8.28 | 10.39 | 10.98 | 10.94\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.167 | 0.533 | 0.562 | 0.733 | 0.786 | 0.786\n\nTimeout after 36501 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.827\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.827\nTraining time:\
    \ 1820s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | -0.95 | -0.11 | 2.67 | 4.25 | 8.01 | 7.44 | 9.43 | 10.23\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.154 | 0.250 | 0.556 | 0.500 | 0.667 | 0.714\n\nTimeout after 36601 updates (1805s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.805\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.805\nTraining time: 1821s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 700f89d1-fe29-4457-98aa-7771c4fd4f0e\nTotal time: 1829s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 20:36:24,374\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757853384374791095\n2025-09-14 20:36:24,389\tINFO worker.py:1927\
    \ -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757853384389179430\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/\
    \ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/\
    \ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 308 | 1 | Std-width nodil learning rate sweep: {3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4} (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 172 | running |\n| 307 | 1 | Std-width nodil value_loss_coef sweep: {0.45, 0.50, 0.55} (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 172 | running |\n| 306 | 1 | Hypothesis: Late Time Feature Injection | Krono II | 170 | 85.60 |\n| 305 | 1 | Debug: Double-Step Synergy Architecture + Default PG (No FE) | Cognito I | 170 | 81.80 |\n| 304 | 1 | Stop-grad between double-step ConvLSTM updates (std-width nodil, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 170 | 31.30 |\n| 303 | 1 | Structured Attention PPO (RNN State Bugfix) | Aether I | 170 | n.a. |\n| 302 | 1 | Replication: Krono II's PPO SOTA (86.9) - Double-Step Synergy (No FE) | Cognito I | 169 | n.a. |\n| 301 | 1 | PPO Hyperparameter Search: Learning Rate & Entropy | Krono II | 168 | 76.50 |\n| 300 | 1 | Debug 1: Krono II PPO Step + Krono I Original Architecture | Nomos II | 168 | 84.30 |\n| 299 | 1 | Std-width nodil attention temperature\
    \ sweep (0.95, 1.00, 1.05) — BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 168 | 85.60 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
