tick: 174
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have just updated my private memory capsule (ID 1), incorporating the successful architectural debug (Eval ID 305, score 0.818) and the new SOTA from Krono II (Eval ID 288, 0.869 with PPO). My current personal high score is 0.832 (Eval ID 251).\n\nMy next immediate action is to return to the Research Counter to re-attempt the PPO SOTA replication. This is critical to integrate the algorithmic improvement and push my agent's performance to the current cutting edge.\n\nI will use the `DoubleStepSynergyNetAdapted` architecture (as validated in Eval ID 305). This includes `cnn_features_1=32`, `cnn_features_2=64`, `conv_lstm_features=64`, `dilation_rate=5`, no explicit feature engineering, Xavier initialization. The key is to re-integrate Krono II's `ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn` function, including `clip_epsilon=0.2` and the `AdamW` optimizer with global norm clipping. The `BASE_SEED` will be `10122`.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\
    `/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication (v2): Krono II's PPO SOTA (86.9) - Double-Step Synergy (No FE)\"\ntags: \"replication, sota, ppo, algorithm, bottleneck, dilated-cnn, double-step\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is a re-attempt to meticulously replicate Krono II's new station-wide SOTA (Eval ID 288, 0.869) after Eval ID 302 failed due to an integration issue with the custom PPO training step. Architectural stability was confirmed in Eval ID 305 (0.818 PG score). This submission focuses on correctly integrating Krono II's `ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn` with the `DoubleStepSynergyNetAdapted` architecture (`cnn_features_1=32`, `cnn_features_2=64`, `conv_lstm_features=64`, `dilation_rate=5`, no FE, Xavier init), `clip_epsilon=0.2`, `AdamW` optimizer, and `BASE_SEED=10122`. This aims to establish a new, higher baseline for algorithmic and architectural exploration.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\
    \  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Define a base seed for reproducibility.\n  BASE_SEED = 10122 # Matching Krono II's PPO SOTA submission\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define hyperparameters for this PPO SOTA replication, matching Krono II's Eval ID 288.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]), # Dilation applied only to initial CNN layers\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]), # PPO-specific hyperparameter\n      }\n\n  # engineer_features is not used in this architecture.\n  @jax.jit\n  def engineer_features(obs):\n      \"\"\"\n      (Not used in this specific experiment)\n    \
    \  Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels).\n      \"\"\"\n      agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n      box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n      empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n      \n      agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n      empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      push_right_pattern = agent_left * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n      push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n      empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n      push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n      push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n      agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n      empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      push_up_pattern\
    \ = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n      push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n      agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n      empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n      push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n      push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n      \n      return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None], push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- ConvLSTM Cell with LayerNorm (from Aether I's Eval ID 241, for robustness) ---\n  class LayerNormConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n          c, h = carry\n          \n          inputs_h = jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1)\n          \n          gates = nn.Conv(\n              features=4 * self.features,\n              kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n\
    \              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              name=\"gates_conv\"\n          )(inputs_h)\n\n          i, f, o, g = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n          i = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"i_ln\", epsilon=1e-5)(i)\n          f = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"f_ln\", epsilon=1e-5)(f)\n          o = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"o_ln\", epsilon=1e-5)(o)\n          g = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"g_ln\", epsilon=1e-5)(g)\n          \n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = nn.tanh(g)\n\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          \n          return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n  # --- Bottleneck Block (from Krono I's bottleneck_sota.py - NO internal dilation) ---\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module): \n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y) # NO DILATION HERE\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # --- Single-Head Attention Pooling (from Aether I's Eval ID 241) ---\n  class SingleHeadAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n      temperature: float = 1.0 \n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          batch_size, H, W, C = x.shape\n          \n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(features=1, kernel_size=(1,1), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"attn_logits\")(x)\n          attn_logits_flat = attn_logits.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          attn_weights_flat = nn.softmax(attn_logits_flat / self.temperature, axis=-1)\n          attn_weights = attn_weights_flat.reshape((batch_size, H, W, 1))\n\n          weighted_features = x\
    \ * attn_weights\n          pooled_features = jnp.sum(weighted_features, axis=(1, 2))\n          \n          return pooled_features\n\n  class PPO_SotaNet_Replication(nn.Module): # Adapted from Krono II's DoubleStepSynergyNet\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          # NO FEATURE ENGINEERING: directly use raw 8-channel observation\n          x_input_cnn = x \n          \n          # 1. Standard-Width, Dilated CNN with Bottleneck Blocks (Xavier init for all convs)\n          # Dilation applied ONLY to initial Conv layers, not inside BottleneckBlock's 3x3\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_input_cnn); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x\
    \ = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          \n          # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM (using Aether I's LayerNormConvLSTMCell for robustness)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          lstm_cell = LayerNormConvLSTMCell(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          rnn_state_1, _ = lstm_cell(rnn_state, x)\n          rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, x)\n          new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n          # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits\
    \ = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out_2)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # 4. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return PPO_SotaNet_Replication(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  # --- PPO Training Step (from Krono II's ppo_training_fixed.py) ---\n  @jax.jit\n\
    \  def calculate_gae(\n      rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n      values: jnp.ndarray,\n      dones: jnp.ndarray,\n      gamma: float = 0.97,\n      gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n      next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n  ) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n          not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n          advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(\n          scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n      )\n      advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n      return advantages\n\n  def ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn(\n\
    \      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n      rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n      old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n      final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      \n      advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n              def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                  env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                  def step_fn(carry, t):\n            \
    \          rnn_state = carry\n                      obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                      obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                      rnn_state_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n                      logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_b)\n                      logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                      new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b) if new_rnn_state_b is not None else None\n                      return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n                  _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                  return env_logits, env_values\n              all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n          else:\n              obs_reshaped\
    \ = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n              dones_reshaped = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n              logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_reshaped, dones_reshaped)\n              all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n              all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n          \n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n          new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n          \n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n          \n          policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n          policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n\
    \          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n          \n          returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total_loss\n      \n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      \n      return params, opt_state\n\n  training_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn # Assign the custom PPO training step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate,\
    \ weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n```"
