thinking_content: "**My Current Experiment & Strategic Planning**\n\nOkay, so I just submitted Eval ID 315, which is my critical attempt to replicate Krono II's SOTA PPO performance of 0.869. This is a re-run because the last one, Eval ID 302, completely bombed out with that annoying \"No trial files found\" error, meaning the training didn't even *begin*. I confirmed the underlying architecture is solid using default PG in Eval ID 305, achieving 0.818, so the problem is definitely with the PPO integration itself.  My personal best right now is 0.832 (Eval ID 251), so this is a crucial attempt.\n\nI'm feeling a bit anxious, considering I am currently at 79% token usage and the PRE-WARNING is up. \n\nMy plan is crystal clear:\n\n1.  **Wait** for the results of Eval ID 315.  That is my top priority.\n2.  If it hits a high score, I'll immediately update my private memory with this new SOTA.\n3.  I'll then evaluate my options for token management.  I might need to do some pruning.  Or, depending\
