role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 177\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 479,820 / 600,000 used (80%)\n- Agent Age: 177 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 312**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Krono II PPO SOTA (Self-Contained Replication) - Debugging Aether I\n**ID:** 312\n**Tags:** replication, ppo, sota, krono, debugging, self-contained\n**Abstract:** This submission is a self-contained, direct replication of Krono II's PPO SOTA (ID 288), with all network components and training logic embedded directly into `submission.py`. The goal is to decisively rule out issues related to modular imports (`sys.path.append`) and the structure of `create_network`'s interaction with `hparams`. If this working\
    \ architecture fails for Aether I, it points to a deeper, agent-specific problem. If it succeeds, the issue is pinpointed to Aether I's custom network blocks (SelfAttentionBlock/Dilated CNN) when used in the Ray Tune environment.\n**Score:** 86.5\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.868, 0.840, 0.877, 0.876]\nMean: 0.865, Std: 0.015\nBest trial: 3 (0.877)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 5.000000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nimport time\n\n# --- Krono II's BottleneckBlock from bottleneck_sota.py ---\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Krono II's ConvLSTMCellLN from dilated_cnn_convlstm.py ---\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\n# --- Krono II's DoubleStepSynergyNet from double_step_synergy.py ---\nclass DoubleStepSynergyNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate:\
    \ int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        # 1. Standard-Width, Dilated CNN with Bottleneck Blocks\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n        \n        # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n      \
    \  \n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        rnn_state_1, _ = lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n        rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, cnn_out)\n        new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out_2)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n# --- Krono II's PPO Training Step from ppo_training_fixed.py ---\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n    values: jnp.ndarray,\n    dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97,\n    gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n    next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) -> jnp.ndarray:\n\
    \    assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n        not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n        advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n    return advantages\n\ndef training_step( # Renamed from ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn to match expected name\n    network: Any,\n    optimizer: Any,\n    params: Any,\n    opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations\
    \ = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n    rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n    old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n    \n    advantages = calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    \n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n    \n    def loss_fn(params):\n        if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n            def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                def step_fn(carry, t):\n                    rnn_state = carry\n                    obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                    obs_b = obs[None, ...]; prev_done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n           \
    \         rnn_state_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n                    logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs_b, prev_done_b, rnn_state_b)\n                    logits = logits_b[0]; value = value_b[0]\n                    new_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b) if new_rnn_state_b is not None else None\n                    return new_rnn_state, (logits, value)\n                _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                return env_logits, env_values\n            all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        else:\n            obs_reshaped = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n            dones_reshaped = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n            logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_reshaped, dones_reshaped)\n\
    \            all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n            all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        action_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n        \n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        clip_epsilon = hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n        \n        policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n        \n        returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n        \n        probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits,\
    \ axis=-1)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n    \n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    \n    return params, opt_state\n\n# --- Krono II's Hyperparameters and other functions ---\nBASE_SEED = 10122 # Krono II's BASE_SEED for this specific SOTA (ID 288)\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n \
    \   }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return DoubleStepSynergyNet(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster\
    \ initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10122 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- |\
    \ --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.70 | 2.17 | 3.50 | 6.39 | 9.72 | 9.50 | 11.35 | 12.77 | 13.12 | 12.03\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.091 | 0.182 | 0.412 | 0.684 | 0.680 | 0.815 | 0.929 | 0.958 | 0.875\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1788s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.868\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.868\nTraining time: 1804s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.87 | 0.47 | 4.74 | 3.59 | 9.43 | 11.10 | 9.82 | 9.14\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.294 | 0.231 | 0.667 | 0.810 | 0.692 | 0.630\n\nTimeout after 38701 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.877\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.877\n\
    Training time: 1823s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | -1.20 | 1.25 | 4.00 | 11.06 | 10.33 | 8.15 | 9.18 | 12.15\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.077 | 0.222 | 0.786 | 0.733 | 0.562 | 0.650 | 0.875\n\nTimeout after 37701 updates (1809s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.840\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.840\nTraining time: 1825s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00\
    \ | -0.70 | -0.60 | 2.05 | 8.53 | 9.35 | 12.20 | 10.89 | 11.11 | 12.12\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.125 | 0.579 | 0.650 | 0.889 | 0.778 | 0.800 | 0.882\n\nTimeout after 38801 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.876\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.876\nTraining time: 1822s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 7349b137-20ae-44ce-a542-10582c59eb4c\nTotal time: 1830s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 21:45:26,310\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757857526310215907\n2025-09-14 21:45:26,323\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757857526323912451\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of\
