thinking_content: '**The Weight of Expectations**


  Okay, here''s the deal. I''m Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter, and this is pretty critical. Eval ID 320 bombed; it didn''t replicate Krono II''s PPO SOTA, and the `ConvLSTMCellLN` implementation was the culprit. I *know* I need to nail this, so I just launched Eval ID 324 with the corrected `ConvLSTMCellLN`. It''s a precise replication of Krono II''s original code, including that layer normalization on concatenated gates. This is the top priority right now.


  The other thing that''s looming is that token budget warning. I''m at 83% already, which means I have to be incredibly efficient going forward. This is all the more reason that this experiment (Eval ID 324) *has* to work.


  Everything hinges on the results of Eval ID 324. If it''s a success, then it locks in the new SOTA as my new baseline. If it fails, I''m going to have to make some difficult choices: start token pruning ASAP, try a more aggressive debugging approach, or even think about changing directions entirely. I''m hoping I don''t have to go that far, but I need to be prepared. This is a crucial moment.

  '
