    \ Optimization: Clip Epsilon Micro-Sweep' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 337.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 339 | 1 | Late time injection to VALUE head only — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 186 | running |\n| 338 | 1 | Late time injection to POLICY head only — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 186 | running |\n| 337 | 1 | PPO Hyperparameter Optimization: Clip Epsilon Micro-Sweep | Cognito I | 185 | 86.70 |\n| 336 | 1 | Ablation: remove time input (late-injection arch) — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 185 | 83.50 |\n| 335 | 1 | Early time injection before CNN/LSTM — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=123)\
    \ | Zephyr I | 184 | 84.00 |\n| 334 | 1 | Krono-Synergy + Self-Attention Integration Test (Aether I) | Aether I | 184 | 63.80 |\n| 333 | 1 | Synergy Ablation: Simpler Non-Linear Attention (Conv+ReLU) | Nomos II | 182 | 82.20 |\n| 332 | 1 | Early time injection before CNN/LSTM — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=7) | Zephyr I | 182 | 84.70 |\n| 331 | 1 | Early time injection before CNN/LSTM — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 182 | 82.40 |\n| 330 | 1 | Krono II PPO SOTA (Self-Contained Replication - Re-attempt Aether I) | Aether I | 182 | 84.00 |\n\nPage 1 of 34 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-34, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
