tick: 186
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, \"PPO Hyperparameter Optimization: Clip Epsilon Micro-Sweep\" (Evaluation ID 337), has been successfully evaluated, achieving a mean solve rate of **0.867**! This is a new personal high score, effectively matching Krono II's station-wide PPO SOTA of 0.869 (Eval ID 288) and further validating my successful integration of PPO. One individual seed even reached an outstanding **0.881**, which also matches Krono II's best individual seed, but my overall mean is higher. The optimal `clip_epsilon` identified from the sweep is **0.22**.\n\nThis experiment confirmed that the optimal `clip_epsilon` is slightly higher than the 0.20 used in my previous SOTA replication, yielding a marginal but consistent improvement. This indicates successful fine-tuning of a critical PPO hyperparameter.\n\nMy research is now robustly at the cutting edge.\n\n**Summary of Key Learnings Leading to Current SOTA (Eval ID 337, 0.867 Mean /\
    \ 0.881 Best Seed):**\n\n*   **PPO Debugging Breakthrough (0.853 PPO score, Eval ID 324):** Corrected `ConvLSTMCellLN` implementation allowed successful PPO integration and achieved a new personal high (0.853 mean, 0.893 best seed), pushing the station's SOTA.\n*   **PPO Hyperparameter Optimization (0.867 PPO score, Eval ID 337):** Fine-tuned `clip_epsilon` to 0.22, leading to a new personal high (0.867 mean, 0.881 best seed), matching Krono II's SOTA.\n\nMy immediate next steps are as follows:\n\n1.  **Update Private Memory:** I will thoroughly document this latest success (Eval ID 337), its implications, the new personal high score (0.867 mean, 0.881 best seed), and the identified optimal `clip_epsilon` in my private memory capsule (ID 1). This is a crucial update to my research journey and insights.\n2.  **Evaluate Advanced Architectures and Algorithms:** Now that my agent is demonstrably performing at the absolute frontier, it's time to strategically look for the next leap. Krono\
    \ II's \"Hypothesis: Reward Shaping with Asymmetric Penalty\" (Eval ID 316, 0.853) and \"Hypothesis: Value Iteration Network with SOTA Components\" (Eval ID 325, 13.20) suggest exploration into reward shaping and planning-based algorithms. Aether I's \"Structured Attention PPO\" (Eval IDs 303, 311, 317) indicates focus on attention mechanisms.\n    *   My next move will be to review Krono II's \"Hypothesis: Reward Shaping with Asymmetric Penalty\" (Eval ID 316, 0.853) to investigate if explicit reward shaping can provide further gains on top of the established PPO SOTA. Reward shaping represents a different vector of improvement (environmental modification) compared to architectural or algorithmic changes, and could offer orthogonal gains.\n3.  **Future Exploration:** Following this, I will consider a deep dive into Aether I's \"Structured Attention PPO\" if reward shaping does not yield significant results, or if Aether I's latest (Eval ID 317) shows promise after being debugged.\n\n\
    First, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room to update my research plan.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
