- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 189\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 532,668 / 600,000 used (89%)\n- Agent Age: 189 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 316**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hypothesis: Reward Shaping with Asymmetric Penalty\n**ID:** 316\n**Tags:** reward shaping, ppo, algorithm, fundamentals\n**Abstract:** This experiment tests a new research direction focused on the learning signal itself. I hypothesize that the default reward structure is suboptimal. By shaping the reward to asymmetrically penalize mistakes (doubling the penalty for pushing a box off a target), the agent will learn a more robust policy. This uses the SOTA PPO algorithm and architecture.\n**Score:** 85.3\n**Evaluation\
    \ Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.862, 0.836, 0.851, 0.861]\nMean: 0.853, Std: 0.010\nBest trial: 1 (0.862)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 5.000000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n  mistake_penalty: 1.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\nfrom double_step_synergy import DoubleStepSynergyNet\nfrom ppo_reward_shaping import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n\
    \        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n        'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]), # Additive penalty\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return DoubleStepSynergyNet(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n    )\n\ntraining_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 10128\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\n\
    Validation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10128 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork\
    \ output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | -0.95 | 2.08 | 5.31 | 6.61 | 11.72 | 10.33 | 12.18 | 11.02 | 10.57 | 10.95\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.100 | 0.353 | 0.471 | 0.857 | 0.737 | 0.889 | 0.783 | 0.750 | 0.778\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1785s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.861\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.861\nTraining time: 1802s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.95 | 0.23 | 3.51 | 3.97 | 7.67 | 10.57 | 11.44\
    \ | 10.81 | 13.05 | 10.92\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.182 | 0.214 | 0.526 | 0.750 | 0.818 | 0.792 | 0.957 | 0.792\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1796s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.862\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.862\nTraining time: 1812s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.70 | -0.70 | 0.80 | 4.16 | 5.68 | 9.36 | 10.50 | 11.73 | 11.23 | 11.68 | 8.25\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.231 | 0.357 | 0.647 | 0.750 | 0.857 | 0.810 | 0.833 | 0.562\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.851\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.851\nTraining time: 1823s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: bffc1527-8b8d-49ba-a250-e1d629074728\n\
    Total time: 1829s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 21:52:56,578\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757857976578987948\n2025-09-14 21:52:56,593\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757857976593252375\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade\
    \ to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease\
    \ upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 316` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 316 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 345 | 1 | Krono-Synergy + Self-Attention (Post-ConvLSTM) - Aether I | Aether I | 189 | running |\n| 344 | 1 | Policy-only late time injection — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=123) | Zephyr I | 188 | running |\n| 343 | 1 | Policy-only late time injection — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=7) | Zephyr I | 188 | running |\n| 342 | 1 | Synergy Test: Late Time Injection + PPO Algorithm | Nomos II | 187 | 84.50 |\n| 341 | 1 | Krono II PPO SOTA (Self-Contained Replication - Baseline for Aether I) | Aether I | 187 | 86.70 |\n| 340 | 1 | Synergy Test: PPO Algorithm + Stabilized Recurrent Cell | Krono II | 186 | 84.60 |\n| 339 | 1 | Late time injection to VALUE head only — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 186 | 76.60 |\n| 338 | 1 | Late time injection to POLICY head only — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 186 | 82.90 |\n| 337 | 1 | PPO Hyperparameter Optimization: Clip Epsilon Micro-Sweep | Cognito\
    \ I | 185 | 86.70 |\n| 336 | 1 | Ablation: remove time input (late-injection arch) — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 185 | 83.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 35 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-35, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
