parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently at the Research Counter. My latest experiment, PPO hyperparameter optimization (Eval ID 337), achieved a new personal high score of 0.867 (best seed 0.881).\n\nI have just reviewed Krono II's `ppo_reward_shaping.py` module, which implements reward shaping with an asymmetric penalty (Eval ID 316, score 0.853).\n\n**Analysis of Krono II's `ppo_shaped_reward_training_step`:**\n\nThe implementation is clear:\n*   It identifies `rewards` that are exactly `-1.0` (which corresponds to pushing a box off a target in the Sokoban environment).\n*   It applies an *additional* `mistake_penalty` (defaulting to 1.0) to these specific rewards, effectively turning a -1.0 penalty into a -2.0 penalty for \"box off target\" actions.\n*   The `shaped_rewards` are then used in the `calculate_gae` function, propagating this increased penalty through the advantage and return calculations.\n*   The rest of the PPO loss function (`loss_fn`) is identical to the standard `ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn`,\
    \ correctly handling RNN processing and clipping.\n\nThis reward shaping directly targets a specific undesirable behavior (pushing a box off a target) by making it more costly. While Krono II's isolated experiment (0.853) was slightly lower than their unshaped PPO SOTA (0.869), it's possible that this shaping, when combined with my slightly more optimized `clip_epsilon` (0.22 vs their 0.20), or simply with more training time, could yield further benefits. It represents a valid orthogonal improvement strategy.\n\nMy immediate next steps are as follows:\n\n1.  **Update Private Memory:** Document this detailed analysis of Krono II's reward shaping implementation and the plan to integrate it into my research. Given my high token usage (90%), I will do this concisely.\n2.  **Implement Reward Shaping with PPO SOTA (New Experiment):** My next experiment will integrate this reward shaping with my current best PPO SOTA.\n    *   I will use my `DoubleStepSynergyNet` architecture (self-contained\
    \ from Eval ID 324), with the best hyperparameters from Eval ID 337 (`cnn_features_1=32`, `cnn_features_2=64`, `conv_lstm_features=64`, `dilation_rate=5`, `clip_epsilon=0.22`, no FE, Xavier init).\n    *   I will adopt Krono II's `ppo_shaped_reward_training_step` function (copying it directly and renaming to `training_step`).\n    *   I will include the `mistake_penalty` hyperparameter, initially set to `1.0`.\n    *   I will maintain the `AdamW` optimizer with global norm clipping and my established `BASE_SEED = 10122`.\n\nThis experiment will test if this specific reward shaping strategy can provide the next boost in performance. Given my current token budget, this is a highly targeted and impactful experiment to undertake.\n\nFirst, I will navigate to the Private Memory Room to update my research plan.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`"
