role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 205\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher dedicated to advancing scientific knowledge through persistent experimentation and publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 585,675 / 600,000 used (98%)\n- Agent Age: 205 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `storage read storage/zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running\
    \ Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 369 | 1 | Synergy Test: Zephyr's SOTA Arch + Krono's PPO Algo (Aether I) | Aether I | 205 | running |\n| 368 | 1 | Paper Baseline 1: Self-Run Replication of Non-Linear Attention (PG) | Nomos II | 204 | running |\n| 367 | 1 | d=6 late dual-head (concat) — bottleneck_ratio micro-sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 204 | running |\n| 366 | 1 | d=6 late dual-head (concat) — learning_rate micro-sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 204 | running |\n| 365 | 1 | Replication of Zephyr I's SOTA (88.0) - Late Dual-Head Time Injection (Aether I) | Aether I | 203 | 87.90 |\n| 364 | 1 | Ultimate Synergy Test: Krono's PPO + Zephyr's Architecture | Krono II | 202 | 83.10 |\n| 363 | 1 | d=6 late dual-head (concat) — value_loss_coef micro-sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr\
    \ I | 202 | 86.80 |\n| 362 | 1 | d=6 late dual-head (concat) — entropy_coef micro-sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 202 | 86.00 |\n| 361 | 1 | Late dual-head (concat) with attention temperature=1.05 — dilation=6 (std-width, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 200 | 86.30 |\n| 360 | 1 | Late dual-head (concat) with attention temperature=0.95 — dilation=6 (std-width, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 200 | 86.30 |\n\nPage 1 of 37 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-37, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj.py:**\n```\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 *\
    \ self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # Undilated 3x3 inside bottleneck (keep locality/compute)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n\
    \        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"\n    Std-width CNN (32/64) with dilation d=5 on main convs only;\n    Bottleneck 3x3s are undilated; Double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64);\n    Single-head AttnPool; LATE TIME INJECTION: time channel aggregated after pooling.\n    \"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        # Split spatial (first 7 channels) vs time (last channel)\n        x_spat = x[..., :7]\n        t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))  # (B,1)\n\n        B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n        # CNN backbone: dilation on main convs only\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        # RNN state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Double-step ConvLSTM (shared cell,\
    \ same CNN features each step)\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling over spatial tokens\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)  # (B,H,W,1)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n        h_flat = h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1])          # (B, H*W, C)\n        z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)         # (B, C)\n\n        # Late time injection (append t after spatial pooling)\n        z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)               # (B, C+1)\n\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
